# =============================================================================
# JARVIS .gitignore
# Tracked: source code, docs, knowledge_base.jsonl, model_catalog.json,
#          .agent/ rules and workflows, learning materials.
# Excluded: regenerable binaries, third-party clones, large static reference.
# =============================================================================

# -- Binary regenerables (rebuild from source code + research papers) ---------
jarvis_data/chromadb/
jarvis_data/chromadb_backups/
jarvis_data/extracted_images/

# ChromaDB persistence created by learning exercises or scratch tests anywhere
# in the tree (sqlite + the UUID-named binary index dirs alongside them)
**/chroma.sqlite3*
**/demo_metadata_db/
**/test_jarvis_persistence_db/
**/*_chromadb/
**/*_chroma_db/

# -- Client work (2026-08-22) -----------------------------------------------
# Verbatim Celebal/BUPA client code + raw project notes. NEVER committed —
# not here, not to a private fork, not anywhere off client infrastructure.
# Top-level and whole-directory on purpose: one unambiguous rule beats a
# gitignored subfolder inside a tracked tree, which leaks the first time
# someone runs `git add -f` or edits the pattern.
# Only GENERALIZED lessons leave this directory, distilled by hand into
# knowledge/Data Engineering/Data_Engineering_Lessons.md.
client_work/

# -- Third-party clones (re-clone fresh on each laptop) -----------------------
# ai_model_repos/OpenClaude and OpenJarvis/ were both DELETED 2026-08-22:
# superseded strategy + completed ports, 173M for provenance alone. Patterns
# kept so a stray re-clone never gets committed. Pinned SHAs for citation
# resolution: OpenJarvis 35b8991cc20b7d636cd65b2728592d2d93bf03cd,
# OpenClaude 877b4dc88600062d8bbfaf764bfbd828c55699e8.
OpenJarvis/
ai_model_repos/
Open-Claude-Cowork/

# -- Large static reference --------------------------------------------------
# Research papers are ~50 MB and almost never change.
# Bulk-copy them once via the HDD's jarvis-bulk/ folder, not via git.
research_papers/

# -- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.eggs/

# -- Node --------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# -- Editor / IDE / OS junk --------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# -- Machine-local operational infrastructure (not part of the synced project)
# /CLAUDE.md (root only) is a Claude Code @import proxy — work-laptop-only.
# Note the leading `/`: without it, this pattern would also gitignore .agent/rules/CLAUDE.md
# which IS supposed to be synced (canonical operating context per the file itself).
/CLAUDE.md
# SYNC.md / RUNBOOK.md were the HDD-era operational docs — superseded by
# GitHub-based sync; kept locally on work laptop for reference.
SYNC.md
RUNBOOK.md
# .agent/ is the per-runtime workflow + rules infrastructure.
# It is now tracked to synchronize rules and workflows across machines.
# .claude/ is Claude Code's per-project settings dir (work-laptop-only;
# personal laptop runs Antigravity, not Claude Code). Machine-local.
.claude/

# -- Legacy / regenerable data files ----------------------------------------
# knowledge.md is the raw source distilled into Data_Engineering_Lessons.md.
# Personal laptop has its own pre-existing copy from the Antigravity-era setup.
jarvis_data/knowledge.md
# model_catalog.json is regenerable via `python3 scripts/sync_openrouter.py`.
# Snapshot goes stale anyway as OpenRouter's catalog evolves.
jarvis_data/model_catalog.json
# compaction_log.jsonl is the machine-local audit trail of kb_compact.py runs.
# Useful for forensics on the local machine; not needed across machines.
jarvis_data/compaction_log.jsonl
# kb_compact.py creates a .bak before any --force write. Machine-local.
jarvis_data/knowledge_base.jsonl.bak

# -- Local secrets / env -----------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
*.local
*.pem
*.key

# -- Build artifacts ---------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# -- Untracked local items ---------------------------------------------------
jarvis_data/openclaude_jarvis_patches.patch
jarvis_data/Q&A/
ollama_models/

.databricks

# Personalization capture buffer (machine-local raw firehose; distilled profile + KB entries migrate instead)
jarvis_data/observation_queue.jsonl

# Cognitive Synthesis Loop — regenerable indexes + local surfacing state (Wave 2, Stage 3.5.10/3.5.7/3.5.11)
# Derived from the queue + KB; rebuildable via correlation.py --backfill / consolidator re-run. The durable
# life_state KB entries (in knowledge_base.jsonl) are what migrate, not these caches.
jarvis_data/behavioral_state_model.jsonl
jarvis_data/life_state_feed.jsonl
jarvis_data/.surfaced_watermark
jarvis_data/.runtime_state.json

# Assembled specialist fine-tuning corpora (Stage 5.2.2) — regenerable via
# jarvis_core/specialists/*_corpus.py from jarvis_core/, KB, chat-history, DE corpus.
jarvis_data/training_corpus/

# Structured cognitive-dimension index (Decision 2026-08-10) — regenerable via
# jarvis_core/memory/cognitive_index.py from knowledge_base.jsonl.
jarvis_data/cognitive_index.sqlite3

# Experience coverage map (2026-08-24) — records what the user HAS and HAS NOT
# worked on professionally. Gitignored for the same reason as personal_life.md,
# but a different risk: a PUBLIC document titled "things this engineer hasn't
# done" is career-sensitive while a job switch is live (knowledge/Job Switch/).
# Flip to tracked once the repo is private — it is high-value migration
# material, just not public-safe today. Hand-authored, NOT regenerable.
jarvis_data/experience_map.md

# Private life notes (2026-08-15) — NOT regenerable, NOT derived from anything else.
# Deliberately kept off the public repo: names real third parties (family, partner,
# friends) who never consented to public visibility. Does not auto-sync to the
# personal laptop under the current all-public-GitHub model — see KB 452 / Stage 6.7.
# Do not delete assuming it can be rebuilt. It cannot.
jarvis_data/personal_life.md

# Terminal conversation memory (machine-local raw transcripts + the current-session
# pointer; NOT synced — only distilled KB entries migrate, like the capture queue)
jarvis_data/.terminal_session.json
jarvis_data/conversations/
